Subject: [PATCH] sycl: GQA flash-decode kernel for 1-8 query tokens (A770)

Extracted from patches/xe1-only-on-top-of-prs.patch at ef777/a770-qwen-xe1 da7f577 2026-10-11:
fattn-gqa-dec.cpp/.hpp and the fattn.cpp hook only (3 of 31 file diffs). The README states
the patches are MIT like llama.cpp; the repo has no LICENSE file. One work-group per KV head
serves all query heads that share it, for q8_0/f16 KV, D=64/128/256, no sinks or softcap.
GGML_SYCL_FA_GQA_DEC=0 turns it off. Author timings are on an A770 under Windows.
Local change: the q8_0 D=256 SLM ESIMD kernel tests mask on the host (has_mask). The in-kernel
64-bit pointer compare made IGC 2.43 emit an unemulated 64-bit shift for acm-g10 ("Q destination
data type is not supported"), which failed the whole ESIMD image for DG2.

